<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<addon
  id="inputstream.airplay"
  version="0.1.5"
  name="AirPlay Receiver"
  provider-name="popcornmix">
  <requires>@ADDON_DEPENDS@
    <import addon="xbmc.python" version="3.0.1"/>
  </requires>
  <extension
    point="kodi.inputstream"
    name="airplay"
    protocols="airplay"
    extension=""
    tags="true"
    library_@PLATFORM@="@LIBRARY_FILENAME@"/>
  <extension
    point="xbmc.service"
    library="default.py"/>
  <extension point="xbmc.addon.metadata">
    <platform>@PLATFORM@</platform>
    <license>GPL-3.0-or-later</license>
    <source>https://github.com/popcornmix/inputstream.airplay</source>
    <assets>
      <icon>icon.png</icon>
    </assets>
    <news>Runs on macOS as well as Linux. The receiver socket and cover art moved into the add-on's own profile directory, so it no longer needs to write to /run. Verbose logging and forgetting paired devices are settings now. Remote control still works with Kodi's remote control service switched off.</news>
    <summary lang="en_GB">Mirror an iPhone or iPad screen to Kodi</summary>
    <description lang="en_GB">Receives AirPlay screen mirroring, video streamed from apps, and audio, and plays them through Kodi's own pipeline, so hardware decoding and the normal renderer are used.

Video protected by DRM cannot be received: the sender blanks it before it leaves the phone.</description>
  </extension>
</addon>
